  setupTitle: 'Setup and support', setupHow: "Set up the app on the user's iPhone",
  setup1: 'On GitHub (easier on a computer): create a new private repository just for this user (for example locatif-sauvegarde-name), ticking "Add a README". Don\'t reuse a test repository.',
  setup2: 'Create a token for their iPhone: Settings › Developer settings › Personal access tokens › Fine-grained tokens › Generate new token. Name it after their phone, pick a long expiry (note the date), "Only select repositories" › the new repository, Permissions › Contents: "Read and write".',
  setup3: 'Choose a new passphrase (at least 12 characters, for example 4 random words) and write it on paper twice: one copy for the user, one for you.',
  setup4: 'On their iPhone: open {url} in Safari, Share › "Add to Home Screen", then always open the app from its icon.',
  setup5: 'In the app: Settings › Automatic backup › "Main phone", the new repository, the token (sent by AirDrop, not by email), its expiry date and the passphrase, then "Connect and back up". Data already entered goes up straight away: check that "Last automatic backup" shows.',
  setup6: 'If a message says the repository already contains a backup, it is the wrong repository: restore nothing, cancel, then "Disconnect" and connect again with the right one.',
  setup7: 'To help them later: create a second token for that repository with Contents "Read-only", then on your device Settings › Automatic backup › "Support copy", same repository and passphrase. The data on your device is then replaced with theirs.',
  setup8: 'Remind them never to delete the app icon (that erases their data) and to keep the passphrase on paper.',
